<%# Overrides Devise's own bare `<p>`-tag default (gem source: devise/app/views/devise/mailer/
    reset_password_instructions.html.erb) — every other mailer in this app (account/agency/
    billing/event/report) composes its body from shared/mailer/_heading, _button, _notice inside
    layouts/mailer.html.erb's own card (that layout's own comment), so a Devise-triggered email
    landing in the same inbox with completely different, unstyled markup would be an obvious
    "which app is this" tell. DeviseMailer (app/mailers/devise_mailer.rb) already renders through
    that same layout (no `layout false` override there, unlike ParticipantMailer's own deliberate
    exception) — only this inner content needed replacing to match.

    @resource/@token are the same ones the stock view uses — Devise::Mailers::Helpers sets both
    before rendering; edit_password_url below is the same helper call the stock view makes too. %>
<%= render "shared/mailer/heading", title: "Reset your password" %>

<div style="color:#686868;padding-top:16px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;">
  Someone requested a link to change the password for <strong style="color:#1f1f1f;"><%= @resource.email %></strong> on xEvent. Use the button below to choose a new one.
</div>

<%= render "shared/mailer/button",
      url: edit_password_url(@resource, reset_password_token: @token),
      label: "Reset Password" %>

<%= render "shared/mailer/notice",
      body: "If you didn't request this, you can safely ignore this email — your password won't change until you open the link above and set a new one." %>
